		<h3>Apple PowerBook G4 1.25 15" (FW800 - Al)  Specs</h3>
		<p class=3D"specstop">Identifiers: 15-Inch FW800 - M8981LL/A - <a class=
=3D"ital" href=3D"https://everymac.com/ultimate-mac-lookup/?identify=3DPowe=
rBook5,2">PowerBook5,2</a> - <a class=3D"ital" href=3D"https://everymac.com=
/ultimate-mac-lookup/?identify=3DA1046">A1046</a> -  <a class=3D"ital" href=
=3D"https://everymac.com/ultimate-mac-lookup/?identify=3D1960">1960</a></p>

	    <p><em><a href=3D"https://everymac.com/systems/apple/powerbook_g4/">Al=
l PowerBook G4 Models</a> | <a href=3D"https://everymac.com/systems/by_year=
/macs-released-in-2003.html">All 2003 Models</a> | <a href=3D"https://every=
mac.com/ultimate-mac-comparison-chart/?compare=3Dall-powerpc-macs&amp;highl=
ight=3D0&amp;prod1=3DPowerBookG413" target=3D"_top">Dynamically Compare Thi=
s Mac to Others</a></em></p>

	=09

<p></p><br>
=09
	<p><img src=3D"https://everymac.com/images/cpu_pictures/apple_powerbook_g4=
_15.jpg" alt=3D"Apple PowerBook G4 15-Inch" width=3D"200" height=3D"148" cl=
ass=3D"comppic">The PowerBook G4/1.25 15" (FW800) features a 1.25 GHz Power=
PC 7447 (G4) processor with the AltiVec "Velocity Engine" vector processing=
 unit and 512k on chip level 2 cache, 512 MB of PC2700 DDR SDRAM, an 80 GB =
Ultra ATA/100 hard drive (4200 RPM), a slot-loading 2X DVD-R/CD-RW "SuperDr=
ive", a Firewire "400" and "800" port, built-in Bluetooth 1.1 and AirPort E=
xtreme (802.11g), and ATI Mobility Radeon 9600 (4X AGP) graphics with 64 MB=
 of DDR SDRAM in an attractive aluminum alloy case with a 15" widescreen TF=
T display (1280x854 native resolution). Custom configurations also were ava=
ilable.<br><br>The PowerBook G4 "Firewire 800" series adds AirPort Extreme =
(802.11g), Bluetooth 1.1, USB 2.0, and Firewire "800", as well as a faster =
logicboard and memory, to the 15" models.<br><br>Please note that unlike th=
e otherwise similar <a href=3D"https://everymac.com/systems/apple/powerbook=
_g4/specs/powerbook_g4_1.0_15.html">PowerBook G4/1.0 15" (FW800)</a>, the P=
owerBook G4/1.25 15" (FW800) <i>has</i> the fiber optic based "ambient ligh=
t sensor" that automatically "measures ambient light and works with integra=
ted software to adjust keyboard illumination and screen brightness based on=
 user preferences". The PowerBook G4/1.25 15" also has a faster processor, =
twice the default RAM, a larger hard drive, a more capable optical drive, a=
nd pre-installed AirPort Extreme (802.11g).<br><br>Also see: <a href=3D"htt=
ps://everymac.com/systems/apple/powerbook_g4/faq/differences-between-12-15-=
firewire-800-17-powerbook-g4.html">What</a> are the differences between the=
 12-Inch, "Firewire 800" 15-Inch, and 17-Inch PowerBook G4 models introduce=
d on September 16, 2003?</p>
=09
	<p><em>Despite the age of this system, site sponsor <a rel=3D"nofollow" hr=
ef=3D"https://everymac.com/owc" target=3D"_blank">Other World Computing</a>=
  has RAM, hard drives, SSDs, and other upgrades available for <a rel=3D"no=
follow" href=3D"https://eshop.macsales.com/MyOWC/Upgrades.cfm?model=3D187" =
target=3D"_blank">this specific Mac</a> while supplies last.</em></p>
